  "2026-08-03T11:15:47.038Z","harness:codex","Attribution sequencing 2026-08-03: fleet analytics cannot be trusted until live-corpus coverage is enforced, resolver failure is distinguishable from unavailable, invalid boolean role values are rejected, non-Claude model and effort adapters work, and topic or role attribution is populated automatically. These are now explicit blockers rather than generic relationships."
  "2026-08-03T11:19:53.252Z","harness:codex","Graph correction 2026-08-03: removed reciprocal blocked_by spellings for pm-lu6sca and pm-eq9dlw because those items already hold the canonical blocks edges to this item. The semantic prerequisite remains; storing both directions added no information and triggered duplicate-edge governance."
  "2026-08-03T11:20:44.252Z","harness:codex","Cycle correction 2026-08-03: removed analytics-side blocked_by mirrors for pm-1wiugq, pm-c0lrdm, and pm-3zgh2c. Canonical direction remains pm-1wiugq blocks the delivery features, which implement this analytics outcome; pm-lu6sca and pm-eq9dlw retain their existing blocks edges. This preserves the prerequisite chain without a reciprocal active cycle."
  "2026-08-06T17:02:10.923Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-06: all-status duplicate search for fleet attribution, harness/model throughput, rework, and defect escape found pm-gw6uyq as the canonical feature; all recorded blockers are live-terminal and pm next reports this item ready. Active scope is bounded read-only SDK/CLI analytics over immutable history, grouped by harness/model/author source with sample counts and honest unavailable/insufficient states."
  "2026-08-06T17:23:03.108Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: fleet analytics now derive observational harness/model/author-source event, close, reopen, throughput, rework, and discovered-from defect-escape projections from immutable history, with unavailable/insufficient states and an explicit non-routing policy."
  "2026-08-06T20:12:21.793Z","harness:codex","Final verification: exact coverage passed across 441 files and 6,902 tests at 100% statements (49461/49461), branches (35933/35933), functions (10115/10115), and lines (47921/47921). TypeScript, ESLint, duplicate detection, 100% docstrings, contracts, SDK surface, package boundaries, SDK parity, token/context/tracker gates, zero-vulnerability audits, and temporary packed npx/direct-SDK/bunx acceptance passed. Timing budgets passed in a clean isolated sample; later host-load samples were invalidated by unrelated system contention without changing budgets."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-06T20:12:06.376Z","harness:codex","Fleet evidence must remain observational: sample denominators, insufficient states, explicit window receipts, and a non-routing policy prevent sparse or unverified identity data from becoming an authorization signal."
